[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 343 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         Set the specified unit properties at runtime where this is supported. This allows changing configuration parameter properties such as resource control  settings  at[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 344 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         runtime.  Not all properties may be changed at runtime, but many resource control settings (primarily those in systemd.resource-control(5)) may. The changes are ap‐[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 345 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         plied immediately, and stored on disk for future boots, unless --runtime is passed, in which case the settings only apply until the next reboot. The syntax  of  the[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 346 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         property assignment follows closely the syntax of assignments in unit files.[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 347 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 348 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         Example: systemctl set-property foobar.service CPUWeight=200[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 349 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 350 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         If  the  specified  unit  appears to be inactive, the changes will be only stored on disk as described previously hence they will be effective when the unit will be[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 351 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         started.[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 352 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K[m
