[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 380 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         Mounts an image from the host into the specified unit's mount namespace. The first path argument is the source image on the host, the second path  argument  is  the[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 381 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         destination directory in the unit's mount namespace (i.e. inside RootImage=/RootDirectory=). The following argument, if any, is interpreted as a colon-separated tu‐[m
[7m Manual page systemctl(1) line 382 (press h for help or q to quit)[27m[K[K [KESCESC[KOO[KBB[K         ple  of  partition name and comma-separated list of mount options for that partition. The format is the same as the service MountImages= setting. When combined with[m
