 [K[31;167H[?2026l[?2026h[H(B[m[38:2:84:92:126m<<<(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m8 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[1;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mprovided when running the script. I aliased it "(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mmytouch(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m" in "~/.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mbashrc(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m"[2;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m9 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[2;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[165X[3;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m10 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[3;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mAnother automation script I had tried is one that I use to run shell scripts and shell commands whose tasks require the banner to be shown in running the output.[3C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::224:175:104m[38:2:192:202:245mits(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m aim is to avoid having to invoke my banner function each time it is needed to be run when running a shell script or shell command needing it. I aliased it "(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mmyrun(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m" (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245min "~/.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mbashrc(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m"[6;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m1 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[6;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[163X[7;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m12 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[7;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried making a shell script to automate seeding my data files. I wanted to be able to whenever necessary, be able to quickly re-seed the needed data files.[7X[8;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m13 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[8;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[14X[9;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m4 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[9;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### Failures and Problems[10;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m5 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[10;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWith the feature to be able to create scripts already having the shebang statement, and (B