ed(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m path, which is what we want[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mto avoid.[35X[18;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m2 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[18;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[161X[19;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m23 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[19;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried escaping the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m$(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m for each variable with (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m\(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m,  it did not work, I in fact got syntax error because of my bad placement of those but even when I did place them    [C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mcorrectly, it did not work. I also tried placing the variable calls in single quotes, that did not help either.[21;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m4[22;4H5 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[22;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWhat eventually did work was using (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mprintf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m with the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m%s(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m option,  and with that I was able to preserve and write those two lines as is.[29X[23;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m26 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[23;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[111X[24;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m7 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[24;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### What I accomplished[25;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m8 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[25;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI managed to successfully complete, test and use my automation shell scripts being my_run.sh and my_touch.sh as well use them for creating other shell script files[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m(module shell scripts so far and the seeding shell script)[27;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m9 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[27;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[23X
