 [81C(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m [38;61H(B[m[38:2:169:177:214m                       [35;10H[?2026l[?2026h[38;61H"logbook.md" 43L, 2832B[35;10H[?2026l[?2026h[38;61H"logbook.md" 43L, 2832B[38;61H(B[m[38:2:26:27:38m                       [35;10H[?2026l[?2026h(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[H[2J(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  15 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[1;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWith the feature to be able to create scripts already having the shebang statement, and (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m import without (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m itself was[6C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mproblematic. Firstly to import (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m without (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to it,  after the shebang statement, I placed the following:(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m-
  16 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[3;7H 
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  18 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[4;7H (B[m[38:2:158:206:106mCURR_SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  19 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[5;7H (B[m[38:2:158:206:106msource "$CURR_SCRIPT_DIR/../etc/naledi.conf"
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  21 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[6;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mInitially, I used the echo command and redirected the output using (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m>(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m to the created shell script. However, the variable calls in those two lines would be written[5C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245minto that file after being expanded out, meaning the path to (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m would be written as is in the new file, resulting in a (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoded(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m path, which is what we want[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mto avoid.
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  22 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[9;7H 
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  23 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[10;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried escaping the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m$(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m for each variable with (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m\(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m,  it did not work, I in fact got syntax error because of my bad placement of those but even when I did place them[5C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mcorrectly, it did not work. I also tried placing the variable calls in single quotes, that did not help either.
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  24 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[12;7H 
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  25 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[13;7H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWhat eventually did work was using (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mprintf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m with the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m%s(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m option,  and with that I was able to preserve and write those two lines as is.
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  26 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[14;7H 
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  27 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[15;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### What I accomplished
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  28 (B[m[38:2:68:157:171m▎[16;7H (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI managed to successfully complete, test and use my automation shell scripts being my_run.sh and my_touch.sh as well use them for creating other shell script files[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m(module shell scripts so far and the seeding shell script)
