                                                                                  [H(B[m[38:2:86:95:137m[48:2:21:22:30m (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30m[1;3H (B[m[38:2:86:95:137m[48:2:21:22:30msession_end.sh [1;20H (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30m▕[1;22H(B[m[38:2:97:131:187m[48:2:21:22:30m▎[1;23H(B[0;1m[3m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30m  (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30m󰍔[1;26H (B[0;1m[3m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30mlogbook.md   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[48:2:21:22:30m[1;41H (B[m[38:2:86:95:137m[48:2:21:22:30m                                          [2;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m13   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[3;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m14   (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### Failures and Problems(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[4;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m15   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWith the feature to be able to create scripts already having the shebang    (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mstatement, and (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m import without (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.    (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m itself was problematic. Firstly to import (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m without          (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoding(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m the path to it,  after the shebang statement, I placed the       (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mfollowing:(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m-(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[9;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m16   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[10;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m8   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106mCURR_SCRIPT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)"(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[11;4H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m9   (B[m[38:2:158:206:106msource "$CURR_SCRIPT_DIR/../etc/naledi.conf"(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[12;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m21   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mInitially, I used the echo command and redirected the output using (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m>(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m to   [K[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mthe created shell script. However, the variable calls in those two lines    (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mwould be written into that file after being expanded out, meaning the path  (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mto (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mnaledi(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mconf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m would be written as is in the new file, resulting in a       (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mhardcoded(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m path, which is what we want to avoid.[K[17;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m22   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K[18;3H(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m23   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI tried escaping the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m$(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m for each variable with (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m\(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m,  it did not work, I in [K[3C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mfact got syntax error because of my bad placement of those but even when I  (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mdid place them correctly, it did not work. I also tried placing the         (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mvariable calls in single quotes, that did not help either.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  24   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  25   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mWhat eventually did work was using (B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mprintf(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m with the (B[m[38:2:122:162:247m[48:2:65:72:104m%s(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m option,  and with   [K[C (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mthat I was able to preserve and write those two lines as is.[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  26   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  27   (B[0;1m[38:2:158:206:106m[48:2:39:45:45m### What I accomplished(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  28   (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mI managed to successfully complete, test and use my automation shell      (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mscripts being my_run.sh and my_touch.sh as well use them for creating other (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mshell script files (module shell scripts so far and the seeding shell       (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mscript)[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  29   (B[m[38:2:192:202:245m[K
(B[m[38:2:59:66:97m  30   (B[0;1m[38:2:255:158:100m- (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mLastly, I achieved completing my shell script for seeding data. Although  (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245mit only seeds herd_registry.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mdat(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m, districts.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mdat(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m and quarantine_zones.(B[m[4:3m[58:2::219:75:75m[38:2:192:202:245mdat(B[m[38:2:192:202:245m     (B[m[38:2:59:66:97m       (B[m[38:2:192:202:245monly so far.[K
